.value_counts()
1.to count gender
print(df['gender'].counts())
note:By default, value_counts() completely ignores missing values (NaN). (we use dropna=False) 
to get percentages, you need to use the normalize=True parameter inside value_counts().
df['region'].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100 (*100 make 0.40=40)
2. how to combine percentages with missing data
print(df['region'].value_counts(dropna=False,normalize=True)*100)

